\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Tonal minimal-pair protection (intra-tone cos $-$ inter-syllable cos) across fingerprint variants on the original $36$ synthesized Vietnamese minimal-pair clips ($6$ carrier syllables $\times $ $6$ tones, $25$ same-syllable tonal pairs after alignment). The 6-d tone-only fingerprint is the only variant with positive protect score ($+0.028$); the full 272-d concatenation and the MFCC-only variant both fail in the wrong direction. The same qualitative ranking is preserved on the expanded $20$-syllable $\times $ $6$-tone $=120$-clip corpus reported in \S  \ref {sec:exp:twostream} and Figure~\ref {fig:minimal_pair_noisy}.}}{10}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
