\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Existence-rule two-stream voting on the expanded $20$-syllable $\times $ $6$-tone $=120$-clip minimal-pair corpus under clean and four additive-noise conditions ($\mathrm  {SNR}\in \{20,15,10,5\}$~dB; synthetic DEMAND-like broadband background, RMS-scaled per clip). Bars show self-lookup recall, correct-miss rate on tonal variants, and false-hit rate at $\tau _A=0.85$, $\tau _B=0.93$. Self-lookup remains at $120/120$ across all conditions; tonal correct-miss varies in $29$--$56\%$, the $36\%$ clean figure exposing that the original $30$-clip subset over-estimated tonal protection.}}{11}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
