\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Six negative results documented to ground each architectural decision. Four are abandoned alternatives; one (\S  \ref {sec:lim:earlyexit}) is a measured behaviour we initially mis-read as a positive speedup before discovering it was repetition-loop suppression; one (\S  \ref {sec:lim:t2collide}) was a diacritic-stripping collision failure mode that we have since resolved with the two-stream AND-gated T2 design (\S  \ref {sec:method:textcache}, \S  \ref {sec:exp:t2v2}).}}{20}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
